cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ISAR in your research, please cite this software."
type: software

title: "ISAR: Inelastic Scattering Automated Researcher"

authors:
  - family-names: Merritt
    given-names: Adrian M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5457-8444"

abstract: >-
  ISAR is a prototype automated pipeline for inelastic X-ray and
  triple-axis neutron scattering experiments: it parses incoming
  scans, analyzes them with per-scan verdicts on how far to trust
  each result, and can drive data acquisition against a simulated
  instrument.

license: GPL-3.0-or-later

repository-code: "https://github.com/ammerritt-gh/ISAR"
url: "https://github.com/ammerritt-gh/ISAR"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23771477"

keywords:
  - inelastic scattering
  - inelastic X-ray scattering
  - inelastic neutron scattering
  - triple-axis spectrometry
  - phonons
  - lattice dynamics
  - spectral fitting
  - autonomous experiments
  - data analysis
